Chapter: DeskBrowserPaneTest
  cites Works chapter GopBrowser
  cites Browser chapter BrowserEvent
  cites UI chapter Event
  cites UI chapter KeyInput
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The desk pane's own job is translation, and translation is what this pins.
 The desk's keyboard answers raw Set-1 scancodes; the browser's
 `map-key-event` compares against `key-*` constants and `char-code` values,
 which is what `poll-key` produces and not what a scancode is. `gbr-mods`
 tracks the modifiers because a Set-1 stream carries them as their own make
 and break codes rather than as a mask.

 Each row feeds a scancode and a modifier mask through the pane's converter
 into the browser's action mapping, so a break in either half shows up as a
 wrong action rather than as a pane that silently ignores a chord. Ctrl+t is
 the one that would have caught a mask that never got set: with mods 0 it
 maps to ActionNone, which is exactly what a pane with no modifier tracking
 would do to every chord a browser cares about.

Section: Test

  act-code : BrowserAction -> Integer
  act-code (a) =
    when a
      is ActionNewTab -> 1
      is ActionCloseTab -> 2
      is ActionFocusAddress -> 3
      is ActionReload -> 4
      is ActionBack -> 5
      is ActionForward -> 6
      is ActionScrollUp -> 7
      is ActionScrollDown -> 8
      is ActionNone -> 0
      is otherwise -> 9

  pane-action : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pane-action (sc) (mods) =
    act-code (map-key-event (event-key-down (poll-key-decode sc mods) mods 0))

  mod-fold : Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mod-fold (mods) (scs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then mods
    else mod-fold (gbr-mods mods (list-at scs i)) scs (i + 1) n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 20 gbr-mod-ctrl))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 20 0))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 17 gbr-mod-ctrl))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 38 gbr-mod-ctrl))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 19 gbr-mod-ctrl))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 72 0))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (pane-action 80 0))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (mod-fold 0 [29] 0 1))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (mod-fold 0 [29, 42] 0 2))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (mod-fold 0 [29, 42, 157] 0 3))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (mod-fold 0 [29, 42, 157, 170] 0 4))
  end
